Quantifiers (and indeed anything else) in an abstraction function only in that 
abstraction, so 1 is wrong and 2 is, while messy, correct.





________________________________
From: Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com>
To: lojban@googlegroups.com
Sent: Sat, October 15, 2011 4:20:05 PM
Subject: [lojban] Embedded bridi and scope

coi lojbo

A fairly simple question: how do embedded bridi interact with scope? Do they 
have their own scope? A motivating example, that if you can answer it should 
answer almost all my questions, is the following:

.i mi ba'o terpa lo nu no da jundi
is equivalent to which of the following:
.i no da zo'u mi ba'o terpa lo nu da jundi
.i mi ba'o terpa lo nu no da zo'u da jundi

Intuition and convenience would say it's the latter, but I am really not 100% 
sure.

mu'o mi'e latros

